diff --git a/docs/settings.md b/docs/settings.md
index 4ff49d6094ea5f01c3fc57437d4413bce13085bc..e02f334c9e5b1c27b2857837a9ade35e66b49cc8 100644
--- a/docs/settings.md
+++ b/docs/settings.md
@@ -132,6 +132,14 @@ A controller's vibration weaker than this stays off, and the rest is spread over
 
 Off by default: each controller is a player as soon as it connects, in the order the system lists them. On: a controller becomes a player only when you press one of its buttons, as the lowest player free, so the players choose their order and how many play. That press also reaches the game. When a game asks for more players than have joined, a prompt over the game waits for the others to press a button; B closes it.
 
+### Mouse camera
+
+Mac only, off by default (`DM_MOUSE_CAMERA`). On: hold the right mouse button over the game and move the mouse to turn the camera; it is the right stick, added to the keyboard's Shift and arrow keys. The pointer stays where it is and hides while the button is held, and comes back when you let go, open the sidebar or switch apps. The left button stays the touch screen.
+
+### Mouse camera speed
+
+How far the stick turns for a given mouse movement, 100 % by default, 25 % to 400 % (`DM_MOUSE_CAMERA_SPEED`). At 100 % about 2,500 points of movement a second turn it fully.
+
 ### Microphone
 
 Mac only, off by default (`DM_MIC`). On: the game hears the Mac's default audio input as the console's microphone. The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time uses it to play the ocarina by voice or whistle. macOS asks for permission the first time a game starts listening; refused, the game hears silence. The level follows the loudest of the last few seconds, and `DM_MIC_GAIN=<x>` in an env file fixes it instead (from upstream PR #1662).
